-Watch the board:
+Watch the board. Everything it prints goes to both the native USB port and
+UART0 (TX on GPIO43, the USB-UART bridge port on most boards), at 115200 baud.
+Generation runs once per boot, so press RST to run it again:
 
 ```bash
-PORT=/dev/cu.usbmodemNNNN   # the port deploy.sh printed
+PORT=/dev/cu.usbmodemNNNN   # native USB; a bridge is e.g. /dev/ttyUSB0
 arduino-cli monitor -p "$PORT" --config baudrate=115200
 ```
 
+`deploy.sh` flashes through the first `/dev/cu.usbmodem*` unless `PORT` is set,
+so set it when the board is on a bridge.
+
+Time a run and record its text, timing and profile in a receipt. The script
+resets the board itself; on a bare USB-UART adapter without reset lines, press
+RST once it starts:
+
+```bash
+uv sync --extra device
+uv run python scripts/benchmark_device.py tinystories --port "$PORT" \
+  --out runs/tinystories-baseline.json --repeat 3
+```
+
 The model payload only needs reflashing after a new export. Firmware-only changes
 can be uploaded without rewriting the model partition.
 
